\section{The hand-off list as step 3 text v39 uses it}\label{S4H:sec:list}
Let $\Gamma_1=(\gamma(t_1)-c_1e_1)/\lambda_1$ as in Theorem~4(c) of \fn{step4_proof.tex}, for every good time $\tau^*$ of base slab~180 and every $S_1$ in the certified set.
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\arabic*)},leftmargin=*]
\item \textbf{(H1)--(H5)} as in Theorem~4(c) of \fn{step4_proof.tex} \tI\ (v3.2 values, unchanged), with the v3.3 additions certified by stages of manifest\_v38 \tC: (H2) tightened, in the variable $f-U_1$ on $y\in[14,60]$, bounds $(3.658\cdot10^{-10},1.777\cdot10^{-9},1.665\cdot10^{-6})$, margins $\times27.34$, $\times562.8$, $\times600.9$ (arb rows, stage 15, carried; \key{results.M9_H2_tightened_fU1}); (H2f) on $[60,700]$, with error $(3.137\cdot10^{-7},1.004\cdot10^{-6},2.436\cdot10^{-6})$, margins $\times3.188$, $\times4.983$, $\times4.106$ (stage 16, carried; \key{results.M9_H2f}); the fixed-$L$ cone family (stages 5--7, carried) with the time ratio H7 re-pinned on \fn{fin13v4c} (stage 8: $\bar a\le2.14039\cdot10^{-7}$, ratio $\le1.6000014\cdot10^{-7}\le1.6001\cdot10^{-7}$, $t^*\ge3.68334\cdot10^{-7}$, margin $\times2.302$; \key{results.H7_fixedL}); the far family at every centre of radius $\ge490\lambda_1$, Lemma~O H4 with minimum margin $\times15.58$ (stage 18, re-pinned on zone~III of chain v37; \key{results.M9_H4_far}).
\item \textbf{(H4) range.} Step~3 v3.3 uses the graph property on $y\in[48,700]$ (v3.2: $[48,350]$). The (H2f) stages evaluate $f$ as a graph over the ray on $x\in[45,725]$, which implies it (\fn{continuation_v39.tex}, item ``(H4) range''); the hand-off list should state the range. \emph{Wording only; not re-checked in this file.}
\item \textbf{(H6), new wording.} $\gamma(t_1)$ is a smooth closed immersed curve, symmetric about the $x$-axis, and it is the time-$t_1$ curve of the maximal smooth CDF flow from $\Gamma_0$; the forcing norm is the one determined by $\alpha(\tau_1)$. \emph{Source:} Theorem C-1 (i), (iv) of \fn{C1_identification_v39.tex} \tH, with the Lean theorems (L1), (L2) \tI\ (read from source at commit \fn{d72b7447}, \emph{not built}), DKS (D1) \tI\ (a step inside the proof of Theorem~3.1, \emph{not re-read}), Lemma (P2-a) \tH, and the certificate $\sup|\tilde\kappa e|\le0.0017429<\frac12$ (margin $\times286$; stage 22, \fn{out_v38/iface/C1_ke.json}) \tC. This replaces step~4's sentences ``it is smooth for $t>0$ by parabolic regularity, and closed and immersed as the CDF evolution of a closed immersed curve \textup{[A]}'' (\fn{step4_proof.tex} l.672) and ``(H6) follows from (b) \textup{[A]}'' (l.131), and the continuation sentences ``continuation uses the literature fact (P1) of step~3 \textup{[A]}'' (ll.130, 336) and ``this is the continuation fact (P1) of step 3, from the literature \textup{[A]}'' (l.370), by Lemma C1:lem:max and Propositions C1:prop:P1, C1:prop:P2 of \fn{C1_identification_v39.tex}. Nothing in it uses step~4's (H6) or step~3's (P1$'$), so there is no circularity.
\item \textbf{(GS), new item.} On $|x|\le60$ (certified on $|x|\le60.25$) the tip arc of $\Gamma_1$ in the step-3 frame is a normal graph $u$ over $S_1$ with
\[\sup|k_{S_1}u|\le0.0065170<\tfrac12\quad(\times76.7),\qquad \sup|u'|\le0.054182<1\quad(\times18.4)\]
\tC\ (Lemma GS-1 of \fn{GS_lemma_v39.tex}; stage 23 of manifest\_v38, \fn{out_v38/iface/GS_tau1.json}, equal to \fn{fix14_interface/GS_tau1.json} apart from args, stage 27). It belongs next to (H1) in the hand-off list. \emph{Step-3 side, for reference:} under the bootstrap, GS improves strictly to $\sup|ku|\le5.3903\cdot10^{-4}$, $\sup|u'|\le0.040936$ on $|x|\le60$ (Lemma GS-2; stage 24, \fn{out_v38/iface/GS_boot_v4c.json}, on the \fn{fin13v4c} production run) \tC. The pinned GS\_boot script is the fix-15 script unchanged: the review items GS-2 (align one cell at $x_{13}$) and GS-6 (factor $(1+2C'/L)^{1/2}$ on $\sqrt{L_{\max}}$) are \emph{not} applied; review fix15 rates both negligible (margins $\times24$ and more), and they stay open as records items.
\item \textbf{Not used by step 3:} the true curve's $k_{\max}$ at $t_1$ (open in step~4, \S``Open items'' O3); Lemma~O H7 and H9 are internal to step~3.
\end{enumerate}
\emph{Remaining step-4 sentences marked \textup{[A]}:} ``$T$ is the maximal time by the step-3 continuation criterion (P1)'' (l.789) and the dependency paragraph (l.791) refer to step~3's own continuation criterion. For step~3 v3.3 this is (P1$'$): DKS 2002 Theorem~3.1 with the regularity lemma U-1 (\fn{U1_regularity_v39.tex}) and Theorem C-1(v); it is not removed by C-1 and keeps its own open items (Lean build, DKS re-read).

