\subsection*{O4. Corrections of text v38 (retag damage of the v38 builder)}
The v38 builder replaced the words ``text v37'' by ``text v38'' everywhere, also inside sentences that report what text v37 printed. Text v39 restores ``text v37'' in: \fn{continuation} ($7.12\cdot10^{-3}$; the withdrawn GS sketch; the difference $177.07$), \fn{U1_regularity} (``had $\sqrt\Lambda\le\sqrt{\Lambda_{\rm bar}}$''), \fn{ei_lemma_v4c} ($\times1.679$; ``Audited since''), \fn{main_v3} (the differences $177.07$, $175.09$), \fn{step3_main} ($0.28578$). The same rule turned \fn{runs/reg_fin13v4b} into \fn{runs/reg_fin13v4c} in \fn{step3_v38_main.tex} (``What remains'', Records), the review reference of \fn{GS_lemma_v38.tex} \S``Review'' into its own successor file (it reviews \fn{fix12_texts/continuation_v37.tex} l.41), and the date line of \fn{lemmaU_v38.tex} into a self-reference. Further v38 slips of the same origin, restored in v39: \fn{lemmaU_v38.tex} printed the sha256 of the first versions \fn{fix10_proofs/G1_export_k2.tex} (\fn{4004a774...}) and \fn{fix10_proofs/U1_regularity.tex} (\fn{827a5f51...}) next to the paths of the v38 copies; the header comment of \fn{ei_lemma_v4c.tex} contained a NUL-delimited builder placeholder instead of the sentence ``the E\_I functions are unchanged from \fn{fin13v4b} ... only term H8 was added'' (a comment, never typeset). All are restored. None of them changes a number or an argument.
